              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "If you are looking to watch **MSNBC** live streaming online for free, it is important to know that the network underwent a major transition. \n\nMSNBC officially rebranded to **MS NOW** *(My Source for News, Opinion, and the World)* after Comcast spun off its cable networks (including MSNBC, CNBC, USA, E!, and Syfy) into a new, independent company called **Versant Media Group**. While the NBC name and peacock logo have been dropped, the programming, anchors, and shows (like *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, and *The Beat with Ari Melber*) remain exactly the same.\n\nThe legal and safe ways to watch or listen to the **MS NOW (MSNBC)** live stream for free, along with other low-cost streaming options, include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Trials on Live TV Streaming Services (Full Live Video)\nIf you want to watch the actual live, 24/7 cable television feed on your computer, phone, or smart TV for free, your best option is to sign up for a **free trial** of a live TV streaming service. Just remember to cancel before the trial period ends to avoid being charged. \n* **YouTube TV:** Typically offers a 5-to-14-day free trial and carries the full live MS NOW channel.\n* **Fubo / Fubo Elite:** Frequently offers a 7-day free trial and includes MS NOW in its base package.\n* **DIRECTV Stream:** Offers temporary free trials for new users and includes MS NOW in its lineup.\n\n### 2. Free 24/7 Live Audio Stream (100% Free)\nIf you do not need the video feed and just want to keep up with the news, you can stream the **entire live broadcast audio for free 24/7**.\n* **TuneIn:** The TuneIn radio app and website host the official, live audio simulcast of MS NOW completely free. \n* **SiriusXM:** Also simulcasts the channel's audio feed (which may require a subscription depending on promotional offers).\n\n### 3. Free Clips on the Official YouTube Channel\nWhile you cannot stream the continuous 24/7 live television broadcast on YouTube for free, the official **MS NOW YouTube channel** is highly active. They upload full-length interviews, news segments, and clips from all major shows almost immediately after they air on television. This is a completely free, legal way to get all the day's main commentary on demand.\n\n### 4. Stream via the Official App or Website (Requires TV Provider)\nIf you\u2014or a family member\u2014already have a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV streaming subscription, you can stream MS NOW for free by logging in with those credentials:\n* Go to the official website at **[ms.now](https://ms.now)** or download the **MS NOW app** on iOS, Android, Roku, or Apple TV.\n* Choose \"Link TV Provider\" and sign in to unlock the unlimited live video stream.\n\n---\n\n*Note: You may encounter third-party websites claiming to offer \"free MSNBC/MS NOW live streams.\" These sites are unofficial, unauthorized, and usually laden with intrusive pop-up ads, redirect loops, and malware. It is highly recommended to stick to official trials, YouTube clips, or the free TuneIn audio stream to protect your device.*",
